OL,3,GNEWSAMPs jostle for slice of #14.6m
OL,4,Afrom axed leisure centre
OL,5,
OL,6,FThree Labour MPs in Bradford have found
OL,7,Fthemselves scrapping it out for a share
OL,8,Fof #14.6m left over from a cancelled
OL,9,Fleisure centre project.
OL,11,FThe Reform UK-led council axed the
OL,12,Flong-planned Squire Lane leisure centre
OL,13,Fproject earlier this year, citing
OL,14,Frising costs.
OL,16,FShipley MP Anna Dixon had backed calls
OL,17,Fto use some of the money to reopen
OL,18,FBingley Pool, while Bradford East MP
OL,19,FImran Hussain said last week he wanted
OL,20,Fa share to help turn a derelict
OL,21,Fbuilding on his patch into a youth and
OL,22,Fcommunity hub.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
